==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*uber}}, from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*upér-}}, a comparative form of ''*upo''.

''Germanic cognates:'' {{cog|osx|oƀar}}, {{cog|nl|over}}, {{cog|goh|ubar}} (whence {{cog|de|über}}), {{cog|non|yfir}} (whence {{cog|sv|över}}), {{cog|got|𐌿𐍆𐌰𐍂}}.

''Indo-European cognates:'' {{cog|grc|ὕπερ}}, {{m|grc|ὑπέρ}}, {{cog|la|super}}, {{cog|sga|for}} ({{cog|cy|gor-}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ˈover/|lang=ang}}

====Adverb====
{{head|ang|adverb}}

# [[over]], [[above]]

====Preposition====
{{head|ang|preposition}}

# {{label|ang|+dative, of a location}} [[over]], [[above]], [[beyond]]
# {{label|ang|+accusative, of motion}} over, [[across]]

====Descendants====
* English: {{l|en|over}}

